Binary Search Tree (BST)

Inorder traversal produces a sorted output because it follows the order:
Left → Root → Right

Time Complexity
Average Case: O(log n)
Worst Case: O(n)
BFS vs DFS
BFS (Breadth-First Search): Traverses the graph level by level
DFS (Depth-First Search): Traverses the graph depth-wise
Use Cases
BFS: Used for finding the shortest path in an unweighted graph
DFS: Used for cycle detection in graphs